%% Fact Book section for Topic 5 — included by content/FB/main.gsm under a "Topic 5" H1.

## T5 · Dates and milestones

::: table | Topic 5 timeline — laws, institutions and data.
@widths 1.8,12.2
@font 9.5
Year | Event
1890 | Guardians and Wards Act
1929 | Child Marriage Restraint Act (girls' age later 16 under MFLO)
1937 | Muslim Personal Law (Shariat) Application Act
1939 | Dissolution of Muslim Marriages Act — judicial divorce
1946 | WHO definition of health as complete well-being
1961 | Muslim Family Laws Ordinance — registration, polygamy permission, *talaq* notice (90 days), orphaned grandchildren
1964 | Family Courts Act
1967 | *Khurshid Bibi* — *khula* recognised by the Supreme Court
1973 | Constitution — Arts 25, 25A (2010), 26, 27, 32, 34, 35, 37(e); reserved seats
1976 | Dowry and Bridal Gifts (Restriction) Act
1979 | Hudood Ordinances (Zina Ordinance)
1981 | Disabled Persons (Employment and Rehabilitation) Ordinance — job quota
1987 | Safe Motherhood Conference, Nairobi — Fathalla, "Why did Mrs X die?"
1989 | Crenshaw coins "intersectionality"; Hochschild, *The Second Shift*
1990 | Collins, *Black Feminist Thought* — matrix of domination; Qisas and Diyat Ordinance
1994 | Lady Health Worker Programme; first women's police stations; Thaddeus and Maine's three delays
1996 | Pakistan accedes to CEDAW (with a declaration)
2000 | National Commission on the Status of Women
2002 | National Policy for Development and Empowerment of Women; 60 NA women's seats and 17 Senate seats restored; 10% federal quota for women
2004 | Criminal Law (Amendment) Act on honour crimes; Punjab girls' stipend; *Saima Waheed* (SC) — adult woman may marry without a *wali*
2006 | Protection of Women (Criminal Laws Amendment) Act — rape moved to the PPC; WEF Global Gender Gap Index begins (Pakistan 112/115)
2008 | Benazir Income Support Programme; Women's Parliamentary Caucus
2010 | Protection against Harassment of Women at the Workplace Act; s. 509 PPC; 18th Amendment (Art. 25A; devolution)
2011 | Acid Control and Acid Crime Prevention Act; Prevention of Anti-Women Practices Act; CRPD ratified
2012 | NCHR Act; NCSW Act; LHWs regularised (Supreme Court); Malala shot (9 October)
2013 | Sindh Child Marriages Restraint Act (18); Sindh Domestic Violence Act
2014 | Balochistan Domestic Violence Act; Malala's Nobel Prize; EU GSP+
2016 | Punjab Protection of Women against Violence Act; honour-killing law (October) after Qandeel Baloch (July); anti-rape amendment; PECA; Sindh Hindu Marriage Act; Digital Rights Foundation helpline
2017 | Hindu Marriage Act (federal); Elections Act (5% tickets; 10% turnout rule); Census; GGGR 143/144 ("second-worst")
2018 | Sindh Home-Based Workers Act; Sindh Maternity Benefits Act; Transgender Persons Act; tribal areas merged with KP; National Nutrition Survey
2019 | Pakistan Maternal Mortality Survey (MMR 186); Punjab Domestic Workers Act
2020 | Enforcement of Women's Property Rights Act; Maternity and Paternity Leave Act; ICT Rights of Persons with Disability Act
2021 | Anti-Rape (Investigation and Trial) Act; KP Domestic Violence Act; FSC: minimum marriage age not against Islam
2022 | Harassment Act amended; Justice Ayesha Malik first woman SC judge; floods (650,000 pregnant women affected)
2023 | Digital Census (241 million; female literacy ~53%)
2024 | Maryam Nawaz first woman chief minister; 11 women win general NA seats
2025 | ICT Child Marriage Restraint Act (18); ICT Domestic Violence Act; HPV vaccine introduced; GGGR 148/148 (56.7%); PECA amended; LFS 2024–25 (female LFPR 24.4%); mobile-internet gap 25% (GSMA)
2026 | GGGR 143/145 (59.5%)
:::

